{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe prior tickets-history reclaim reported a fresh-clone ceiling from `.git/objects/pack/*.pack` only. The rewritten baseline tree itself was already 290,690,203 logical bytes, while the incident investigation on `absurd-zoometric-bobwhite` measured a fresh single-branch clone at 322.57 MiB of pack data, 827,550,463 logical checkout bytes, 1,116,577,792 allocated checkout bytes, and 1,475,424,256 allocated bytes for the whole clone. Operators therefore need one reproducible report that cannot conflate Git packing with checkout residence or filesystem block slack.\n\nA fixed footprint ceiling is explicitly out of scope. Closed bug `bardic-continuous-asianlion` records that a monotonically growing tickets pack ceiling repeatedly blocked every unrelated Gerrit change; `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:397-407` preserves the decision to remove that gate. The operator reaffirmed on 2026-08-23 that hard budgets or shrink-only ratchets introduce unacceptable fragility and workflow friction.\n\n## Approach\nAdd an explicit, opt-in, read-only `rebar tracker-footprint` command backed by a reusable measurement module. It will never run implicitly from ticket writes, reconciliation, plan/completion gates, Gerrit Verify, or ordinary `rebar metrics`.\n\nDefault mode measures the configured mounted tracker and identifies when its Git object database is shared, so local object bytes are not misrepresented as a standalone clone. `--fresh-clone` resolves the configured tickets remote and branch, creates a temporary unfiltered single-branch/no-tags clone with local hardlink optimization disabled, measures it, and removes only that command-owned temporary directory. Both text and schema-validated JSON output report the measured ref/tip and definitions alongside values.\n\nThe report separates: packed object bytes; checkout logical bytes; checkout allocated bytes when the platform exposes `st_blocks`; file count and allocation slack; Git-directory logical/allocated bytes; and whole-clone logical/allocated bytes. Unsupported allocation accounting is a structured unavailable value, never a fabricated zero. Size is descriptive only: no threshold, pass/fail classification, baseline mutation, alert side effect, or nonzero exit caused solely by a large result.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/footprint.py`: reusable filesystem/Git measurement and explicit temporary fresh-clone orchestration.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/tracker_footprint.py`: read-only CLI adapter and text/JSON rendering.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/tracker_footprint.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`, and packaged help: register the opt-in command without adding it to write/init paths.\n- `src/rebar/schemas/tracker_footprint.schema.json` and `src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py`: machine-readable output contract.\n- Focused unit/interface/schema/CLI-registry tests and generated `docs/cli-reference.md`.\n- `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md`, and `docs/scale-envelope.md`: define each layer and correct the pack-versus-clone operational guidance.\n\nOut of scope: any budget or ratchet, any CI/Gerrit gate, any scheduled or automatic trigger, any tracker/remote mutation, producer retention changes, or history reclaim.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: measure a temporary standalone tickets clone containing ordinary files; assert exact file count/logical bytes, nonnegative allocation fields, pack bytes, tip, and whole-clone arithmetic through both the library and CLI JSON surface.\n- Discriminating fixture: many one-byte files produce a small Git pack but materially larger checkout allocation; assert the report exposes both values without a failure verdict.\n- Shared-object edge: point default mode at a linked worktree; assert it marks the Git database shared and does not label shared object bytes as standalone-clone bytes.\n- Platform edge: simulate missing `st_blocks`; assert allocated/slack fields are structured unavailable while logical metrics remain exact and exit zero.\n- Failure path: an invalid remote/branch fails before reporting success and removes only its command-owned temporary directory.\n- Regression: existing CLI registry, output-schema coverage, generated help/reference, lint, typecheck, and default tests remain green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar tracker-footprint --fresh-clone --output json` reports separately named pack, checkout-logical, checkout-allocated, file/slack, Git-directory, and whole-clone layers for the measured tickets tip; verified by the focused interface test and JSON-schema validation.\n- [ ] A fixture whose pack is small while small-file allocation is materially larger reports both exact observations and no threshold verdict; verified by the discriminating integration test.\n- [ ] Mounted linked-worktree mode labels shared-object scope honestly, and a platform without `st_blocks` returns structured allocation-unavailable values rather than zero; verified by focused edge tests.\n- [ ] The command is read-only and opt-in: focused tests prove source refs, tracker HEAD/worktree, and remote refs are unchanged, and repository search confirms no invocation from write, reconcile, gate, or CI paths.\n- [ ] User and reuse documentation distinguishes pack, logical checkout, allocated checkout, and whole-clone claims; verified by generated-reference drift checks and documentation tests.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the default test suite pass with no fixed footprint threshold or workflow gate introduced.","title":"Report whole tickets-store footprint beyond Git pack bytes"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787527199064012001,"uuid":"add73d54-4891-4c3f-8af3-7d7dabdf0ed1"}